<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Cookie Policy for FC Mobile Tools by TanzimFC.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / COOKIES</p>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>

    <section><h2>1. What cookies are</h2><p>Cookies are small pieces of information stored in a browser by a website or third-party service. Similar technologies can include local storage and other browser-side mechanisms.</p></section>

    <section id="privacy-choices"><h2>2. Privacy choices and consent</h2><p>The shared privacy-controls component lets visitors accept optional analytics and advertising storage, reject those optional categories, or save separate choices. Where the component is available, it stores the choices in a <code>fcmobiletools_consent</code> cookie with a version and timestamp for approximately 180 days. The shared layout sends the saved preferences to Google's consent signals, including analytics and advertising-related storage and usage settings.</p><p>Consent signalling is not the same as blocking every third-party resource request. Google Analytics and Google advertising scripts may still be requested by the page, and providers may process limited requests under their own consent-mode implementation. Older standalone pages and embedded third-party services may use separate integrations. Use the controls shown on the page where available, and review the relevant provider policies for more detail.</p></section>

    <section><h2>3. Analytics cookies and similar technologies</h2><p>FCMOBILETOOLS uses Google Analytics on pages where the Google tag is installed. It can measure page views, general usage, and technical information through cookies or similar technologies when permitted by the relevant consent settings. The shared layout sets non-essential Google storage to denied by default and updates consent signals according to the visitor's saved choice. This does not mean all Google requests are blocked when storage is denied.</p></section>

    <section><h2>4. Authentication cookies and sessions</h2><p>The private admin and creator workspaces use session cookies to keep authorized users signed in. These are operational and security cookies for restricted areas rather than public advertising cookies. Public account authentication may also store session state through the browser storage used by the authentication service. Sessions expire or can be ended by signing out; clearing cookies or browser storage may sign you out or prevent certain account features from working.</p></section>

    <section><h2>5. Local storage and feature data</h2><p>Some tools and older features store preferences, predictions, progress, quiz state, or similar information in browser storage. Signed-in features may also use browser storage to maintain authentication state. Account quests and related features can keep server-side activity, survey, voting, progression, and reward records as described in the <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>; these records are not necessarily removed when you clear your browser data.</p></section>

    <section><h2>6. Third-party resources and advertising</h2><p>Pages may request resources from Google Analytics, Google advertising services, Google Fonts, Cloudflare, Supabase, Cloudinary, or other service providers. Embedded video, images, and external links can also connect your browser to YouTube, Discord, X, EA, or other platforms. Google advertising may use cookies or similar technologies according to the consent signals, regional requirements, ad settings, and Google's policies. Third-party services can receive technical request information when your browser contacts them, and their own policies govern their processing.</p></section>

    <section><h2>7. Managing cookies and storage</h2><p>You can block, delete, or manage cookies and local storage through your browser settings. Some private authentication and site functionality may stop working correctly if required cookies or browser storage are blocked or cleared.</p></section>

    <section><h2>8. Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy when our analytics, authentication, tools, hosting, or third-party integrations change. The date above identifies the current version.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
